@@ -104,7 +104,7 @@ Every packet has one absolute three-second receipt-to-verdict deadline measured
 
 `PendingUdpVerdicts` owns a joined pump that batches up to 1,024 terminal requests, locks backend write → correlator cell, and releases the backend lock before endpoint kernel handoff. Synchronous backend work uses `block_in_place` on multi-thread runtimes and runs inline on current-thread runtimes. The pump retains direct/block leases across caller cancellation; it rechecks original deadlines at dequeue, after backend locking, after grace and before each item, expiring late requests without conn mutation. A Direct request is late, and expires unarmed, once its deadline leaves less than its activation needs, which comes after the rest of the batch's commit and the release of the originals of every flow the batch arms: a 300 ms margin; the commit work of the batch's requests still to visit, itself included, at the slower of a moving average per request (from the batch's first visit until its armed flows can be activated) and the batch's own rate so far; and the activation work of the flows armed before it and of those still to visit, at a moving average per flow (without the waits for the backend); at least half the hold, since under load the work and waits between arming and activation outgrow what the measured work foretells, and at most all of the hold but the margin, so that a flow fresh from the queue is always armed and the averages stay current. The batch's armed flows then accept their held originals off the backend lock, oldest first, and one backend acquisition activates every flow whose originals are out; a flow whose originals arrived meanwhile goes round again. Cancellation waits for armed Direct completion under that same deadline.
 
-A watchdog checks held cells independently and enforces the hard hold bound, and drains the scheduled cleanups, bounded by the queue's length: a flow cleanup settles its cell, and token cleanups go to the backend together, up to a retirement batch under one fence/grace. The watchdog waits neither for the backend nor for another drainer, and retires a batch a tick, so its pause before scanning the holds is one grace period at most. While the commit pump has work, the pump retires the token cleanups itself, a batch after each of its own, when none of its flows is armed, waiting its turn for the backend as for its commits: readers taking the backend in turn would leave a drain that only tries no turn, and a retirement elsewhere could hold the backend from an armed flow's activation. Stale token, endpoint-generation, or backend-state mismatches drop without mutating a newer incarnation. A verdict failure or any failure after Direct has armed is process-fatal because userspace can no longer safely infer which originals the kernel accepted.
+A watchdog checks held cells independently and enforces the hard hold bound, and drains the scheduled cleanups: a flow cleanup settles its cell, one per cell, and token cleanups, bounded by the queue's length, go to the backend together, up to a retirement batch under one fence/grace. The watchdog waits neither for the backend nor for another drainer, and retires a batch a tick, so its pause before scanning the holds is one grace period at most. While the commit pump has work, the pump retires the token cleanups itself, a batch after each of its own, when none of its flows is armed, waiting its turn for the backend as for its commits: readers taking the backend in turn would leave a drain that only tries no turn, and a retirement elsewhere could hold the backend from an armed flow's activation. A token cleanup only hastens the retirement of staging the kernel keeps fenced by its token: one the full set has no room for, when flows are shed faster than they can be retired, is left to the staging's expiry, 120 s after the flow's first packet, and the janitor, as the staging of a packet the kernel's queue dropped is, and counted (`cleanupFull`); the flow's packets are queued and dropped until then. Stale token, endpoint-generation, or backend-state mismatches drop without mutating a newer incarnation. A verdict failure or any failure after Direct has armed is process-fatal because userspace can no longer safely infer which originals the kernel accepted.
 
